== verdict material (columns only; the judgement is claude-lab's) ==
note, why (b)=0 and (c) is large: Julia f32 and the fixtures are bit-identical (no rounding difference of its own).
  Julia f64 is one path in f64; Python f64 is another rounding of the same f32 weights, and in c a 1-ulp change
  of one weight moves the f64 run by ~1e-4 in step 1 (measured, chaotic). So (c) ~1 cannot be read as a port difference.
